**Goal** — Create `src/workflow/decisions-sidecar.ts` with the sidecar types, entry parsing/validation, merge, timestamp and atomic read/write helpers that both `record` and `promote` share.

**Motivation** — The decisions sidecar is hand-written today: one session wrote `outcome: "promoted"` minutes before the PR was ready, with zero-padded timestamps, and nothing validates an entry's `id` against what the run actually left open.

**Approach** — One sidecar belongs to a run: `.nax/features/<feature>/workflow/<runId>/decisions-<timestamp>.json`, written next to `result.json`. Its shape is `DecisionsSidecar`; the `reasons` field copies the run's `reasons` and `artifact` is `<runId>/result.json`. An entry's `kind` uses the sidecar vocabulary: an open item of kind `ruling` is an `advisor` entry and every other item kind maps to itself. `fixed` requires `sha`; `waived`, `confirmed`, `overridden` and `verified` take none. Every entry is validated before anything is written. Writes go to a temporary file in the same directory and are renamed over the target, so a reader never sees a partial file (mirror the temp-file-then-rename pattern and the injectable `_resultDeps = { mkdir, readdir, rename, stat }` seam in `src/workflow/result.ts`). The directory is git-ignored (`**/.nax/features/*/workflow/`); the commands leave the file uncommitted.

An entry's `id` must name an open item of the run (`LoadedRun.openItems`), with one exception: an entry of kind `ci` or `minor` may carry an id that is not an open item, because the finishing tool tracks live CI checks and fix-now minors that `verdict.openItems` does not list. Any other unknown id is an error naming the open ids.

Every validation failure throws a `NaxError` with code `WORKFLOW_DECISIONS_INVALID` and the messages the ACs give.

**Scope** — In: the new module `src/workflow/decisions-sidecar.ts` and its unit tests. Out: run loading (`loadRunVerdict`), PR reads, CLI commands, and checklist tick/comment text (US-002 to US-005).

**Interface**
```typescript
// workflow/decisions-sidecar.ts  (US-001)
export const DISPOSITIONS = ["fixed", "waived", "confirmed", "overridden", "verified"] as const;
export type Disposition = (typeof DISPOSITIONS)[number];
export const SIDECAR_OUTCOMES = ["pending", "promoted", "verified-ready", "abandoned"] as const;
export type SidecarOutcome = (typeof SIDECAR_OUTCOMES)[number];
export const SIDECAR_KINDS = ["finding", "advisor", "gate", "ci", "story", "cannot-verify", "minor", "reason"] as const;
export type SidecarKind = (typeof SIDECAR_KINDS)[number];

export interface DecisionEntry {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly kind: SidecarKind;
  readonly disposition: Disposition;
  /** One non-empty line. */
  readonly reason: string;
  /** 7 to 40 hex characters; required when disposition is "fixed". */
  readonly sha?: string;
}

export interface DecisionsSidecar {
  /** "<runId>/result.json" */
  readonly artifact: string;
  readonly feature: string;
  /** UTC ISO-8601 with ":" and "." replaced by "-", e.g. "2026-10-13T09-12-00-417Z". */
  readonly resumedAt: string;
  readonly reasons: readonly string[];
  readonly decisions: readonly DecisionEntry[];
  readonly outcome: SidecarOutcome;
  readonly url?: string;
}

export function parseDecisionEntries(raw: unknown): DecisionEntry[]; // throws NaxError WORKFLOW_DECISIONS_INVALID
export function sidecarKindFor(item: OpenItem): SidecarKind; // "ruling" -> "advisor"; every other kind maps to itself
export function checkEntriesAgainstItems(entries: readonly DecisionEntry[], items: readonly OpenItem[]): void; // throws NaxError WORKFLOW_DECISIONS_INVALID
export function mergeDecisions(existing: readonly DecisionEntry[], incoming: readonly DecisionEntry[]): DecisionEntry[];
export function isoStamp(date: Date): string; // the resumedAt / file-name timestamp form
export function sidecarFileName(date: Date): string; // "decisions-<isoStamp>.json"
export async function newestSidecar(runDir: string): Promise<{ path: string; sidecar: DecisionsSidecar } | null>;
export async function writeSidecar(path: string, sidecar: DecisionsSidecar): Promise<void>; // temp file then rename
```
`OpenItem` (read only, `src/workflow/types.ts`): `{ id; kind: "finding" | "ruling" | "cannot-verify" | "gate" | "advisor" | "story" | "ci" | "reason"; severity?; file?; line?; issue; suggestion?; ruling? }`.

**Goal** — Move run loading into `src/workflow/run-verdict.ts` (`loadRunVerdict`), add `readPrState`, `WorkflowForgeDeps`, and the `nax workflow record` subcommand that validates rulings against open-item ids and writes/updates the decisions sidecar.

**Motivation** — The decisions sidecar is hand-written and nothing validates an entry's `id` against what the run actually left open; `record` makes the sidecar writer a validated command.

**Approach** — Move run loading, unchanged in behaviour and error messages, from `src/cli/workflow.ts` (file-local `newestResult`, `fillStoryStates`, `notStarted`, `noResult`; `reportFor` builds `openItems` as `verdict?.openItems ?? buildOpenItems(filled)`) to `src/workflow/run-verdict.ts`. `LoadedRun.record` is the record as stored, and `LoadedRun.openItems` is built from the record with `storyStates` filled, as `status` does today. `reasons` is `record.reasons`. `loadRunVerdict` validates the feature name, takes the newest readable run, and throws the same `no workflow result for feature <feature>` and `workflow for <feature> has not started its feature steps (run <runId>)` errors as today. `workflowStatusCommand` builds its report from `loadRunVerdict`; its output and exit codes do not change.

`registerWorkflowCommand(program: Command, deps: WorkflowCliDeps = _workflowCliDeps, forgeDeps: WorkflowForgeDeps = _workflowForgeDeps): Command` registers `status`, `record` in that order (and later `promote`). A caller passing only `deps` (the existing tests) keeps working.

`WorkflowForgeDeps` and `_workflowForgeDeps` are new in `src/cli/workflow-forge.ts`: in this story `WorkflowForgeDeps` has `forge: ForgeDeps` and `now: () => Date` (US-004 adds `waitForChecks: typeof waitForChecks`). The real object uses `defaultForgeDeps` and `() => new Date()`. HEAD is never read in this story. IMPORT RULE: `src/cli/workflow-forge.ts`, `src/cli/workflow-record.ts` and the workflow modules import the workflow leaves by relative path and `src/cli/workflow.ts` only by `import type` (the `@/workflow` barrel loads `step-context`, which imports `@/cli`); `workflow/git.ts` must not be value-imported from `src/cli`; `bun run check:import-cycles` must stay clean.

`record` CLI: `nax workflow record -f <feature> [--decisions <file>] [--outcome <outcome>] [-d, --dir <path>] [--json]`. `--dir` defaults to `process.cwd()` and is the project directory, as for `status`. `--json` prints exactly one JSON object on stdout; on an error it prints `{"error":"<message>"}` on stdout, and without `--json` the message goes to stderr through `deps.logErr` (the `status` convention).

Validation order, each step running only when the earlier ones passed: (1) the feature name; (2) at least one of `--decisions` and `--outcome` given, else `nothing to record: pass --decisions or --outcome`; (3) `--outcome`, when given, is one of `pending`, `promoted`, `verified-ready`, `abandoned`, else `outcome must be one of pending, promoted, verified-ready, abandoned`; (4) `loadRunVerdict`; (5) the decisions file, when given, is read and parsed (`cannot read decisions file: <path>`, `decisions file is not valid JSON: <path>`), its array validated by `parseDecisionEntries` and checked by `checkEntriesAgainstItems`; (6) for `--outcome promoted` or `--outcome verified-ready`, the record has a `url` (`cannot record outcome <outcome>: the workflow result has no PR url`), a forge is detected (`no forge detected for <dir>`) and `readPrState` reports the PR as not a draft (`cannot record outcome <outcome>: PR is still a draft`); (7) the write. The decisions file is a JSON array of entries, not an object. Step 7 loads the newest sidecar of the run: with none, it creates one (`outcome` is `--outcome` or `pending`, `resumedAt` is `isoStamp(forgeDeps.now())`, `url` is the record's `url` when it has one); with one, it merges the incoming entries by id (`mergeDecisions`), applies `--outcome` when given and keeps everything else, and rewrites the same file. `--outcome` with no `--decisions` and no existing sidecar fails with `no decisions sidecar for run <runId>; pass --decisions`. An outcome of `promoted` or `verified-ready` also stores the record's `url`. Exit `0` on success, `1` on any error. After a successful write, `unruled` lists the open item ids that have no entry in the sidecar; it does not change the exit code.

Plain output: `<feature>: recorded <n> decision(s) in <sidecar path relative to dir>; outcome <outcome>`, then `unruled: <ids joined by ", ">` when any. `--json` prints `WorkflowRecordReport`.

`readPrState` runs the forge `view` argv (`viewArgv`; GitHub: `gh pr view <ref> --json isDraft,body,url`) and normalises GitHub (`isDraft`, `body`, `url`) and GitLab (`draft` or `work_in_progress`, `description`, `web_url`) output. Failure handling: `readPrState` cannot read the PR (non-zero exit, unparseable output) -> exit 1 with `cannot read PR <ref>: <detail>` (code `WORKFLOW_PR_READ_FAILED`). Invalid feature name, no workflow run, run not started -> exit 1 with `status`'s messages; nothing read or written beyond that. `record`: nothing to record, bad outcome, unreadable or invalid decisions file, invalid entry, unknown id, kind mismatch -> exit 1 with the message; the sidecar is not created or changed. `record --outcome promoted`/`verified-ready` while the PR is a draft, has no url, or no forge is detected -> exit 1; the sidecar is not created or changed.

`record` checks only what its outcome names: for `promoted` and `verified-ready`, that the PR is not a draft. It does not re-run the `promote` checks; a human recording an outcome is trusted. The open items `record` compares against come from `LoadedRun.openItems` (the run's recorded verdict).

The record tests build their `WorkflowForgeDeps` by spreading `_workflowForgeDeps` and overriding `forge` and `now`, so a field US-004 adds needs no test change. Export the new command symbols (`workflowRecordCommand`, `WorkflowRecordOptions`, `WorkflowRecordReport`, `WorkflowForgeDeps`, `_workflowForgeDeps`) from `src/cli/index.ts`. Update the `workflow-status.test.ts` AC-15 registration test from `["status"]` to `["status", "record"]`. Add the `### nax workflow` section to `docs/guides/cli-reference.md`, covering `status` and `record`.

**Scope** — In: run-verdict.ts, pr-state.ts, workflow-forge.ts (forge + now only), workflow-record.ts, registering `record`, barrel exports, status refactor with no output change, docs. Out: `promote` command, `waitForChecks` on `WorkflowForgeDeps`, checklist tick / evidence comment (US-003 to US-005). Also out: `record` validating that a `fixed` sha's commit exists, or checking that a `ci`/`minor` entry exists; concurrent record calls are not serialised.

**Interface**
```typescript
// workflow/run-verdict.ts
export async function loadRunVerdict(dir: string, feature: string): Promise<LoadedRun>;
export interface LoadedRun {
  readonly runId: string;
  readonly runDir: string;
  readonly result: WorkflowResultFile;
  readonly record: WorkflowFeatureRecord;
  readonly openItems: readonly OpenItem[];
  readonly reasons: readonly string[];
}

// workflow/pr-state.ts
export interface PrState { readonly isDraft: boolean; readonly body: string; readonly url?: string }
export async function readPrState(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string, deps: ForgeDeps, cwd: string): Promise<PrState>; // throws NaxError WORKFLOW_PR_READ_FAILED

// cli/workflow-forge.ts
export interface WorkflowForgeDeps { forge: ForgeDeps; now: () => Date; /* US-004 adds: waitForChecks: typeof waitForChecks */ }
export const _workflowForgeDeps: WorkflowForgeDeps;

// cli/workflow.ts
export function registerWorkflowCommand(program: Command, deps: WorkflowCliDeps = _workflowCliDeps, forgeDeps: WorkflowForgeDeps = _workflowForgeDeps): Command;

// cli/workflow-record.ts
export interface WorkflowRecordOptions { dir: string; feature: string; decisions?: string; outcome?: string; json: boolean }
export interface WorkflowRecordReport { feature: string; runId: string; sidecar: string; outcome: SidecarOutcome; decisions: number; unruled: readonly string[] }
export async function workflowRecordCommand(opts: WorkflowRecordOptions, deps: WorkflowCliDeps, forgeDeps: WorkflowForgeDeps): Promise<number>;
```
Read-only symbols used: `buildOpenItems`, `readResult`, `runDirsNewestFirst`, `storyStatesFrom`, `workflowFeatureDir`, `validateFeatureName`, `detectForge(deps: ForgeDeps, repoRoot: string): Promise<ForgeKind | null>`, `viewArgv(forge, branch, githubFields)`, `defaultForgeDeps`, `ForgeDeps { run(cmd, { cwd, timeoutMs? }): Promise<{ exitCode; stdout; stderr }>; readText }`, and the US-001 module (`parseDecisionEntries`, `checkEntriesAgainstItems`, `mergeDecisions`, `isoStamp`, `sidecarFileName`, `newestSidecar`, `writeSidecar`).

**Goal** — Create `src/workflow/promote.ts` with the pure functions `tickChecklist`, `evidenceComment`, `editBodyArgv`, `commentArgv` and `markReadyArgv`, and break the import cycle `safeInline` would close.

**Motivation** — Promotion mechanics (ticking the checklist by the exact `**<id>**` token, one evidence comment, forge argv) are prose an agent re-derives on every run.

**Approach** — These functions are pure: they take a PR body or entries and return text or argv, and run nothing. `src/workflow/pr-body-safe.ts` imports `escapeInline` and `escapeTableCell` from the `@/finish` barrel, which loads `src/finish/context.ts` and its `@/cli` import; switch that import to the leaf `../finish/pr/escape` (which has no imports) so `promote.ts` can use `safeInline` without closing a runtime cycle. Behaviour of `pr-body-safe` is unchanged.

**Checklist tick.** `tickChecklist` changes only the first line of an entry that matches `- [ ] **<id>**` exactly (the id compared as a plain string, so `B1` never matches `**B10**` and ids such as `_run:ci` need no escaping), turning `[ ]` into `[x]` and appending to the end of that line one of: ` — fixed in <sha>`, ` — verified`, ` — confirmed`, ` — waived: <reason>`, ` — overridden: <reason>`. Indented continuation lines, already-ticked lines and every other line are returned unchanged, and an entry whose id has no checklist line is ignored.

The checklist line format comes from `openItemLine` in `src/workflow/pr-body.ts` (not exported): each unresolved entry renders as `- [ ] **<id>** (<tags>) ...`, optionally followed by indented `  Suggestion:` / `  Advisor:` lines; a gate item renders as `- [ ] **<id>** (gate) — ...`.

**Evidence comment.** `evidenceComment` returns `## Resolved before ready`, a blank line, then one line per entry: `- <id> (<kind>) <disposition>: <reason>`, with ` (<sha>)` appended for a `fixed` entry. The id, the kind and the reason each pass through `safeInline`, and the tick suffixes ` — waived: <reason>` and ` — overridden: <reason>` pass the reason through it too. GitHub uses `gh pr edit <ref> --body <body>`, `gh pr comment <ref> --body <text>` and `gh pr ready <ref>`; GitLab uses `glab mr update <ref> --description <body>`, `glab mr note create <ref> -m <text>` and `glab mr update <ref> --ready`.

`safeInline(text, max?)` (`src/workflow/pr-body-safe.ts`) returns redacted, `@`/`#<digit>`-neutralised, one-line text.

**Scope** — In: `src/workflow/promote.ts`, the `pr-body-safe.ts` import change, unit tests. Out: reading the PR, running forge commands, the `promote` CLI command and sidecar I/O (US-004, US-005). Edits to the PR body beyond the first line of matched checklist entries are not offered.

**Interface**
```typescript
// workflow/promote.ts  (US-003)
export function tickChecklist(body: string, entries: readonly DecisionEntry[]): { body: string; ticked: string[] };
export function evidenceComment(entries: readonly DecisionEntry[]): string;
export function editBodyArgv(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string, body: string): string[];
export function commentArgv(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string, text: string): string[];
export function markReadyArgv(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string): string[];
```
`DecisionEntry` comes from `src/workflow/decisions-sidecar.ts` (US-001).

**Goal** — In `src/cli/workflow-promote.ts`, make `--yes` with both checks passing run the `tick`, `comment`, `ready` and `record` actions in that order, stopping at the first failing action.

**Motivation** — Ticking the checklist, posting one evidence comment, and marking the PR ready are prose steps the nax-finish skill re-derives by hand on every run.

**Approach** — With `--yes` and both checks passed, the actions run in this order, stopping at the first failure: `tick` (read the PR body again with `readPrState` immediately before writing, run `tickChecklist` over the newest sidecar's entries, and write it with `editBodyArgv` only when at least one line ticked; otherwise `skipped`), `comment` (one `evidenceComment` posted with `commentArgv`; `skipped` when the sidecar has no entries), `ready` (`markReadyArgv`), `record` (upsert the newest sidecar to `outcome: "promoted"` with the PR `url`, creating an empty-decisions sidecar when the run has none; use `writeSidecar`, `newestSidecar`, `isoStamp(forgeDeps.now())`, `sidecarFileName`). A non-zero exit from a forge command fails the action with `promote stopped at <action>: <stderr or exit code>`, exits `1`, and leaves the sidecar's outcome as it was. A successful `--yes` run exits `0` with `promoted: true` and a report whose `actions` lists each `PromoteAction` with status `done` or `skipped`. Without `--yes`, or with any check failed (exit 2), no forge write happens and the sidecar is not touched, even with `--yes`.

Failure handling: `promote --yes`: a forge write fails -> exit 1 at that action; earlier actions stay done; the sidecar is not marked `promoted`. A re-run before `ready` succeeded ticks idempotently and posts a second evidence comment; once `ready` has succeeded, a re-run exits 1 with `PR is already ready` and the recovery is `nax workflow record --outcome promoted`. `promote` overwrites the sidecar's `outcome` (including `abandoned`) with `promoted` on success.

Plain output with `--yes`: one line per check, then one line per action, then the result line. Extend the `promote` text in `docs/guides/cli-reference.md` with the actions.

All US-005 tests use the draft-run fixture from `test/helpers/workflow-promote-fixture.ts` (created by US-004) with every check passing unless an AC says otherwise.

**Scope** — In: the four `--yes` actions in `workflow-promote.ts`, the docs extension. Out: validation and checks (US-004, already done), the pure helpers (US-003, consumed as-is). Also out: de-duplicating evidence comments, verifying the head at `ready` time, and serialising concurrent record/promote calls.

**Interface**
```typescript
// consumed from workflow/promote.ts (US-003)
export function tickChecklist(body: string, entries: readonly DecisionEntry[]): { body: string; ticked: string[] };
export function evidenceComment(entries: readonly DecisionEntry[]): string;
export function editBodyArgv(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string, body: string): string[];
export function commentArgv(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string, text: string): string[];
export function markReadyArgv(forge: ForgeKind, prRef: string): string[];

// workflow-promote.ts types (from US-004)
export interface PromoteAction { name: "tick" | "comment" | "ready" | "record"; status: "done" | "skipped" }
export interface WorkflowPromoteReport { feature: string; runId: string; url: string; dryRun: boolean; promoted: boolean; checks: readonly PromoteCheck[]; actions: readonly PromoteAction[] }
```
